### Section 5.4: the natural gradient on the two-dimensional Poisson case.
###
### PINN demo: two-dimensional Poisson with a source term.
###   u_xx + u_yy = f(x,y),   f = -2 pi^2 sin(pi x) sin(pi y)
### on the unit square, with u = 0 on the boundary.  The exact solution
### is u = sin(pi x) sin(pi y).
###
### The residual is written as  u_xx + u_yy - f = 0, so the SRC term
### carries the coefficient -1.  A SRC term makes the collocation file
### hold one extra column, the value of f at that point, placed right
### after the coordinates.  The last column here is the exact solution,
### which Exact_solution 1 reports on but never trains against.
Output_deriv 1 /
Init_w       Glorot_norm
Rand_seed    20260730 / fixed seed (reproducibility)
Restart      0 /
Nlayer       4 / L
2 / ndim(1): (x,y)
20 /
20 /
1 / ndim(L)
Loss_term  DATA         160  data.dat     1.d0  / boundary condition
Loss_term  COLLOCATION  400  colloc.dat   1.d-3 / interior residual
Residual 3 /
LIN   1.d0    2 0 /  u_xx
LIN   1.d0    0 2 /  u_yy
SRC  -1.d0        /  minus the source column of colloc.dat
Exact_solution 1 /
Hod_check 1 /
Num_validation 30 /
Validation_cyc 200 /
P_max          500 /
Epoch      2000 /
Activation TANH /
Conv       1.d-12 /
Num_batch  40 /
Checkpoint_cyc 5000 /
Hod_K      2 /
1.d0
0.d0
0.d0
Hod_dense  1 /
GD_method  Natural_grad
GD_param   1.0d0 1.d-5 0.d0 0.d0 0.d0 /
